      "explanation": "<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l5mkc6w5/9bcd3b0f-bd25-4002-a7df-7f91aec78977/7ac1c150-044b-11ed-b6d5-555c254d75e0/file-1l5mkc6w6.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l5mkc6w5/9bcd3b0f-bd25-4002-a7df-7f91aec78977/7ac1c150-044b-11ed-b6d5-555c254d75e0/file-1l5mkc6w6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2022 (Online) 24th June Evening Shift Chemistry - Chemical Equilibrium Question 54 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l5mkc6w5/9bcd3b0f-bd25-4002-a7df-7f91aec78977/7ac1c150-044b-11ed-b6d5-555c254d75e0/file-1l5mkc6w6.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l5mkc6w5/9bcd3b0f-bd25-4002-a7df-7f91aec78977/7ac1c150-044b-11ed-b6d5-555c254d75e0/file-1l5mkc6w6.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l5mkc6w5/9bcd3b0f-bd25-4002-a7df-7f91aec78977/7ac1c150-044b-11ed-b6d5-555c254d75e0/file-1l5mkc6w6.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l5mkc6w5/9bcd3b0f-bd25-4002-a7df-7f91aec78977/7ac1c150-044b-11ed-b6d5-555c254d75e0/file-1l5mkc6w6.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l5mkc6w5/9bcd3b0f-bd25-4002-a7df-7f91aec78977/7ac1c150-044b-11ed-b6d5-555c254d75e0/file-1l5mkc6w6.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l5mkc6w5/9bcd3b0f-bd25-4002-a7df-7f91aec78977/7ac1c150-044b-11ed-b6d5-555c254d75e0/file-1l5mkc6w6.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Here 2 moles of N<sub>2</sub> also present that is why 2 moles always have to add in total mole calculation.</p>\n<p>At equilibrium,</p>\n<p>Pressure (P) = 2.46 atm</p>\n<p>Volume (V) = 200 L</p>\n<p>Temperature (T) = 600 K</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><s